            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can't fully reproduce the issue:\r\n- Yes, executing `vii` (with 'mini.indentscope' default config) does put cursor on the first non-blank character of the last line.\r\n- No, executing `vai` also puts cursor on the first non-blank character of the last line.\r\n\r\nSo I don't see this as an inconsistency issue within 'mini.indentscope'.\r\n\r\nFurthermore:\r\n- Yes, built-in textobjects do seem to place cursor at the end of textobject when visually selecting. **But** this accounts for selection type: charwise, linewise, blockwise. If you use built-in charwise object (like `vi)`), then it will place cursor at the last character. If you use built-in linewise (like `vip`), then it will place on the first column of the last line.\r\n- No, not all textobjects put cursor at the end of textobject during selection. 'mini.ai' made a conscious decision to put cursor at the start of the object to be more aligned with how cursor is treated after applying operator on textobject/motion (see second paragraph of `:h operator-doubled`).\r\n\r\nHaving this in mind, I'll revisit it later to possibly update to be more align with 'mini.ai' design.",
